{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# DELETE the dormant inbound absence-probe port\n\n**Decision (operator ruling, recorded on this ticket): DELETE.** This ticket is no longer\nan open delete-vs-re-home question; it executes the deletion. Option 2 (re-home the port\nto `binding_walk`) is a REJECTED alternative, retained below only so the rejection is\nlegible.\n\n## What is being deleted, and why it is safe\n\nBug `3b5f-1b21-ee14-4bdf` removed every consumer of the `(inbound, probe)` chain — the\nproducer `differ._compute_mutations_emit_absent_partner_probes`, the dispatch arm\n`_run_differs_inbound_probe_dispatch`, and `reconcile_helpers.route_inbound_probe`. What\nremained is a capability with **zero callers**:\n\n* `_backend.SupportsAbsenceProbe` (Protocol) and the three `probe_remote` implementations\n  (`adapters/jira/backend.py`, `adapters/jira_datacenter/backend.py`,\n  `adapters/jira_datacenter/transport.py`)\n* the neutral vocabulary module `inbound_probe.py` (`ProbeBranch`, `ProbeResult`,\n  `ProbeConfigError`)\n* the Cloud probe `adapters/jira/probe.py` and the shared classifier\n  `adapters/jira_family/probe.py` (`classify_probe_response`), whose only callers are the\n  `probe_remote` implementations above\n\nThis is a **pure deletion with no behavior change**: nothing in a reconcile pass reaches\nany of it. Deletion detection is NOT affected — it lives OUTBOUND, in\n`outbound_differ._safe_get_issue` + `binding_walk`, and the separate **outbound** probe\nleaf (`_apply_outbound_probe`, the `(outbound, probe)` dispatch arm) is live and is NOT\ntouched by this ticket.\n\n## Why option 2 (re-home to `binding_walk`) is rejected\n\n* The port must NOT be used to restore same-pass re-creation — an earlier operator ruling\n  on `3b5f` is that a confirmed-deleted issue is never resurrected. That removes the\n  port's original purpose.\n* Its stated motivation was false: `binding_walk` already takes the direct-GET as an\n  INJECTED `probe_get: Callable`, with `outbound_differ._safe_get_issue` as a lazy default\n  only — there is no hardcoded private reach for the port to fix.\n* It would re-cross an ownership boundary ADR 0028 deliberately draws: absence-vs-deletion\n  discrimination is OUTBOUND-owned. Re-homing an INBOUND port there re-splits what `3b5f`\n  just consolidated.\n* The vocabularies are incompatible in an unsafe direction: `ProbeBranch` has no\n  confirmed-404 branch, and its `ARCHIVED_OR_MOVED` conflates deletion with a\n  still-alive MOVE — routing it to `binding_walk`'s tombstone could tombstone a live\n  moved issue.\n\n## Explicitly OUT of scope (follow-up, not this change)\n\nDeleting the classifier orphans the operator-facing `jira.resolved_statuses` /\n`reconciler.resolved_statuses` config keys and the DC transport's `_resolved_statuses`\nplumbing. Removing DOCUMENTED config keys is a user-visible surface change needing its own\ndeprecate-vs-remove decision, so it is deliberately deferred to a follow-up ticket linked\n`discovered_from` this one — the same reasoning by which `3b5f` deferred this ticket. The\nkeys keep their current behavior here (they simply have no reader), so this change stays\nbehavior-neutral.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] no live caller of the port remains, proven by BOTH a Serena semantic search AND a\n      plain string grep (per AGENTS.md, an empty semantic result alone is not trustworthy),\n      with the evidence recorded as a comment on this ticket\n- [ ] `SupportsAbsenceProbe` and all three `probe_remote` implementations are deleted\n- [ ] `inbound_probe.py`, `adapters/jira/probe.py` and `adapters/jira_family/probe.py` are\n      deleted, and `classify_probe_response` is dropped from the `jira_family` package\n      exports\n- [ ] the **outbound** probe leaf (`_apply_outbound_probe`, the `(outbound, probe)`\n      dispatch arm) is untouched, proven by the existing suite staying green\n- [ ] epic `e369`'s AC5 is amended to drop the probe classifier from its \"one shared\n      implementation imported by both backends\" clause, with the amendment recorded on\n      `e369` and this ticket linked to it\n- [ ] the dormancy notes in `inbound_probe.py`, `SupportsAbsenceProbe` and ADR 0028 are\n      removed along with the code they describe, and ADR 0035 / ADR 0055 no longer list\n      the deleted units as shared\n- [ ] the stale `reconcile_helpers.py` docstring claim that it by-path loads\n      `inbound_probe.py` is corrected (no such runtime load exists)\n- [ ] a follow-up ticket for the orphaned `resolved_statuses` config keys is filed and\n      linked `discovered_from` this ticket\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck` and `make test` are green, and the change is\n      `Verified +1` on Gerrit"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785903499227512001,"uuid":"3615aa4e-2331-4067-acff-700dd43ce9fe"}